  "articleBody": "Getting ready for a roof flashing inspection doesn't have to be complicated, but a little preparation can make the process smoother and help your roofing professional do the best job. Flashing is super important for protecting your home from leaks around chimneys, vents, and other roof interruptions, so it's worth taking a moment to get things in order before we arrive.\n\n### What to Prepare Before You Start\n\n**Clear Interior Access:** If you've noticed any water stains or dampness inside your home, especially in the attic or around ceilings, make sure those areas are accessible. Move any stored items that might be blocking a view of the underside of your roof deck. This helps us see if water has been getting in and where it might be tracking.\n\n**Exterior Clearance:** If possible and safe, clear away any debris from around the base of your chimney, skylights, or other areas where flashing is visible from the ground. Trim back any tree branches that are right up against your roof, as they can obstruct views and even cause damage.\n\n**Note Down Observations:** If you've seen any specific issues, like bent metal, gaps, or rust around your flashing, jot down where and when you noticed them. Even a rough sketch or a quick photo on your phone can be super helpful for pointing us in the right direction. This includes any recent heavy rains or wind events that might have preceded new symptoms.\n\n**Be Ready to Discuss History:** If you know when your roof was last inspected, repaired, or replaced, or if you've had previous leak issues, share that information. Understanding your roof's history helps us interpret current conditions and potential weak spots. This is especially true for homes in the DFW area and surrounding Texas communities that face harsh weather.\n\n**Ensure Safe Access:** While we'll handle the actual roof work, making sure gates are unlocked and pets are secured can help our team get started efficiently and safely. We're fully insured, so you have peace of mind when we're on your property.\n\nBy taking these small steps, you help us efficiently assess your roof's flashing and provide you with honest recommendations. For a reliable roof flashing inspection, contact Discounted Roofing Co. at (254) 205-7067.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}